Z||000001||87FieroGTx||10-29-2001||03:53 PM|||| With the average driver a manual will be faster until you get around 300-400hp then the auto will be faster.  Why you ask? With a manual and 400hp it's very hard to hook up with a auto it's much easier. <P> Even some of the manual 3.4 and 3.8 guys are having a hard time hooking.<P> But lets be real here how many of us are going to have a 300-400hp fiero)<P> <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-29-2001||04:00 PM||||i do... (at the crank)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  my auto hooks up WAY better than the 4:10 i had in the 86 SE... my 60' times are better.. i drive it to work everday with one lazy foot.. and sip my coffee... <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst-schoolgirl.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst-schoolgirl.jpg</A> <P>clutches seemed to fail in my SE quite often... but the auto i've beat the CRAP out of and yeah it's whining but it's still moving on along...<P>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91<P> <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com</A>  - underconstruction - but check it out anywho...||||reg||1
