Z||000005||Fiero_24||10-29-2001||05:13 PM||||I am running a 3 speed auto, and I only like stick shift.  The only reason I took the auto is to run NOS.  After talking with 1FST2M6 I dedcided on the auto.  I know you are only looking for basic info on the 2, but here are my 2 cents.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||10
Z||000006||NOS3800||10-29-2001||06:46 PM||||The other thing you have to consider is the auto is much more consistent when bracket racing. My auto is fine when I don't spray, no tire spin which leaves me to believe I should swap it for a 4T60E out of a GrandPrix GT, taller first gear! but when I spray, I have a HELL of a time controlling wheel spin. It spins through first and tachs out. I have to let off so I don't hit the rev limiter and blow the motor. I have been working on controlling it the past two times at the track, but not quite there. Have had a couple 13.2's and a 13.1 all with tire spin. I have one last chance to beat 1FST2M6's 12.9 before the season is over!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000007||85ZainoGT||10-29-2001||09:09 PM||||so, not much of a difference on stock 2.8's?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> heh||||reg||1
Z||000008||87FieroGTx||10-30-2001||12:13 AM|||| On a stock car the Manuals are a lot faster. I don't have the numbers but I think the manual fiero is around 1 sec faster in the 1/4 STOCK but once you start upping that power the auto comes into it's own.<P> Just think about this I beat a 400hp 99 Trans Am stoplight to stoplight with my stock 86 Why? He had a manual and spun his tires a good 100feet.<P> A average driver will almost always spin there tires in a manual 300-400hp car It takes a great driver who knows how to feather the clutch and hookup.<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75 shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.8 13.9 1/4||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierobear||10-30-2001||01:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>i do... (at the crank)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  my auto hooks up WAY better than the 4:10 i had in the 86 SE... my 60' times are better.. i drive it to work everday with one lazy foot.. and sip my coffee... <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I drive auto with two feet. Much quicker braking.||||reg||1
